Origin:
Allwinner A733 (sun60iw2) and the Orange Pi Zero 4: the clock control unit,
the pin controller, an SD/MMC controller variant, Ethernet glue for the
DesignWare EQOS core, the thermal sensors, the watchdog and device trees.
With these the board boots from microSD to multi-user with gigabit
Ethernet. The register map was read on the board and agrees with the
vendor kernel. The clock and reset numbers are those of the Linux binding
allwinner,sun60i-a733-ccu (v3, September 2026), whose headers are imported
unchanged.

The boot loader leaves the SD card write threshold enabled, and the first
write through the internal DMA never completes; the A733 variant of
sunximmc clears it on host reset.

The EQOS core reports version 5.3, which the driver now accepts. The MAC
address is derived from the chip ID. The RGMII delays in the board tree
are the middles of the windows measured on the board.

The thermal sensor controller has the register layout the H6 introduced,
which sunxithermal(4) does not know, so it has a driver of its own. The
conversion constants, the sampling timing and the place of the calibration
codes in the EFUSE are those of the vendor kernel; the codes and the
readings were checked on the board. sunxisid(4) now reads any EFUSE word
for other drivers, and the Ethernet glue takes the chip ID through it.

The watchdog has the sun20i registers four bytes lower, as on the A523.
On the board it reset the system after its tickling process was killed,
and the system booted again.

The pin controller of the always-on domain keeps the older, denser
register layout; the pin driver takes the layout from the controller's
entry. Its PM1 pin enables the AIC8800D80 wireless module on the second
SD/MMC controller. With both described, the module answers on SDIO as
manufacturer 0xc8a1, product 0x82 with two functions. It has no driver.

mcommphy(4) kept a register code where it expects microamperes and then
reported its own default as an unknown drive strength, which counted as a
hardware detection error on every boot. The default is now "not given",
which selects the same code silently.

